  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nWarm temperatures and dry conditions are expected through Monday. A \npotent low moving across the southern Great Plains will send a cold \nfront through South Texas around Tuesday, though there is still \ndisagreement on the timing and southern extent of the front. As \nthings currently stand, it looks like rain chances will increase \nlate Monday night into Tuesday, with a medium to high chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms along the Coastal Bend and northern \nCoastal Plains. The best dynamics continue to remain north of the \narea, but there could be an occasional strong to severe thunderstorm. \nWe'll continue to monitor the trends. \n\nWill have to continue to monitor the possibility for minor coastal \nflooding along Gulf facing beaches into the weekend, as well as an \nincreased rip current risk.",
